"""Backend of the Post-processing generator page (generators/postProcessGenerator.html).

The page works on maps that already exist in the scene -- the selected maps,
or else the last generated one (tp3d.currentMap). Jigsaw and sliding puzzle
pieces never count. Every tool the sidebar's Post-Process section offers
(Color by Height, Contour Lines, Magnet Holes, Dovetails, Bottom Mark,
Text / SVG import, 2D Heightmap) can be applied from the page; each Apply
changes the real objects right away and re-sends the scene as GLB for the
page's 3D viewer.

Undo is our own (PostProcessSession._undo_stack), not Blender's: before an
action, every object the page shows is copied (object + mesh data + paint
texture pixels); undoing swaps the copies back in with ID.user_remap, so
anything pointing at the objects (tp3d.currentMap, a contour piece's PARENT,
...) follows along.

Everything here runs on Blender's main thread, from
operators.TP3D_OT_post_process_generator.modal().
"""

